<Tunnel title="Format the Second USB | Save My Gig!" status="Critical_Path · Second USB" red>
  <div class="review-flag">DRAFT — review pending. Remove this flag after approval.</div>

  <div class="step-label">Step 1 of 2</div>
  <h2 style="margin-bottom:1rem">Format the second USB</h2>

  <p>Good news: your original drive stays untouched. We prepare the second drive for the CDJ.</p>

  <div class="panel panel-warn">
    <p style="margin:0">⚠️ <strong>This erases everything on the SECOND drive.</strong> Make sure nothing important is on it.</p>
  </div>

  <ul class="checklist">
    <li>Plug the <strong>second</strong> USB into the computer.</li>
    <li>Right-click the drive → <strong>Format</strong> (or use Disk Utility / Disk Management).</li>
    <li>Format: <span class="mono">FAT32</span> · Scheme: <span class="mono">MBR</span> · Quick format: OK</li>
  </ul>

  <p class="question">Is the second USB formatted?</p>

  <a href="/protocol/critical/second-usb-copy" class="btn btn-go" data-event="step_completed" data-step="second_usb_format" data-answer="yes">
    🟢 Yes — formatted
  </a>
  <a href="/protocol/critical/copy" class="btn btn-stop" data-event="step_completed" data-step="second_usb_format" data-answer="no">
    🔴 No — it won't format
    <small>Back to plan A: temporary copy using your original drive.</small>
  </a>
</Tunnel>
